==Abstract==

This LIP defines the '''MWEB descriptor''' function <code>mweb(...)</code> and its allowed encodings, with strict parsing and canonicalization rules. It extends the output script descriptor language to MWEB wallets.

==Motivation==

MWEB wallets need a compact, deterministic way to represent their capabilities in a descriptor string. Such a representation must unambiguously distinguish:

* '''Ranged''' descriptors (covering all subaddresses).
* '''Single-subaddress''' descriptors (covering one specific subaddress).

and must support both '''spend-capable''' (secret key) and '''watch-only''' (public key) forms.

==Specification==

===Function signature and allowed forms===

Valid forms are:

* <code>mweb(master_scan,master_spend,*)</code>
* <code>mweb(master_scan,master_spend,&lt;i&gt;)</code>
* <code>mweb(master_scan,subaddr_spend)</code>

====Ranged (all subaddresses)====

<pre>
mweb(master_scan,master_spend,*)
</pre>

Semantics:
* Identifies (and optionally spends) '''all''' MWEB outputs for the wallet.
* <code>master_spend</code> MAY be a secret key (spend-capable) or public key (watch-only).

====Single (known subaddress index)====

<pre>
mweb(master_scan,master_spend,<i>)
</pre>

Semantics:
* Identifies (and optionally spends) MWEB outputs for exactly one subaddress, specified by index <code>&lt;i&gt;</code>.
* <code>master_spend</code> MAY be a secret key (spend-capable) or public key (watch-only).
* <code>&lt;i&gt;</code> is a decimal, non-negative integer subaddress index.

====Single (unknown index, subaddress spend key known)====

<pre>
mweb(master_scan,subaddr_spend)
</pre>

Semantics:
* Identifies (and optionally spends) MWEB outputs for exactly one subaddress '''without''' explicitly encoding its index.
* <code>subaddr_spend</code> MAY be a secret key (spend-capable) or public key (watch-only).
* This form is used when the '''master spend key''' or the '''subaddress index''' is not known/available, but the '''subaddress spend key''' is.

===Parameter rules===

====Parameter 1: master_scan====

* The first parameter is always the '''master scan key (scalar)'''.
* '''Never''' a master scan public key.
* Encoded using a <code>KEY</code> expression (see [[#Key encoding (KEY expressions)|Key encoding]]).

====Parameter 2: spend key (master_spend or subaddr_spend)====

The meaning of the second parameter depends on form:

* In 3-parameter forms:
** <code>mweb(master_scan,master_spend,*)</code>
** <code>mweb(master_scan,master_spend,&lt;i&gt;)</code>
** The second parameter is always '''master spend''' key material (secret or public).

* In the 2-parameter form:
** <code>mweb(master_scan,subaddr_spend)</code>
** The second parameter is always '''subaddress spend''' key material (secret or public).

====Parameter 3: selector (* or &lt;i&gt;)====

* In ranged form, the third parameter is the literal <code>*</code>.
* In indexed single form, the third parameter is the literal <code>&lt;i&gt;</code> where <code>i</code> is a decimal integer:
** Example: <code>mweb(...,...,17)</code>

===Key encoding (KEY expressions)===

All key-like parameters (<code>master_scan</code>, <code>master_spend</code>, <code>subaddr_spend</code>) are encoded using the standard <code>KEY</code> expressions defined in [https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0380.mediawiki BIP 380]. In summary, a <code>KEY</code> expression consists of:

* Optionally, key origin information, consisting of:
** An open bracket <code>[</code>
** Exactly 8 hex characters for the fingerprint of the key where the derivation starts (see BIP32 for details)
** Followed by zero or more <code>/NUM</code> or <code>/NUM'</code> path elements to indicate unhardened or hardened derivation steps between the fingerprint and the key or xpub/xprv root that follows
** A closing bracket <code>]</code>
* Followed by the actual key, which is either:
** A hex encoded public key (66 characters starting with <code>02</code> or <code>03</code> for a compressed pubkey, or 130 characters starting with <code>04</code> for an uncompressed pubkey).
** A WIF encoded private key, with the same meaning as the corresponding public key.
** An <code>xpub</code> encoded extended public key or <code>xprv</code> encoded extended private key (as defined in BIP32).
*** Followed by zero or more <code>/NUM</code> unhardened and <code>/NUM'</code> hardened BIP32 derivation steps.
*** Optionally followed by a single <code>/*</code> or <code>/*'</code> final step to denote all (direct) unhardened or hardened children.
*** The usage of hardened derivation steps requires providing the private key.

(Anywhere a <code>'</code> suffix is permitted to denote hardened derivation, the suffix <code>h</code> can be used instead.)

X-only public keys (64 hex characters) are '''not''' permitted inside <code>mweb</code>.

===Derivation relationship===

If <code>master_scan</code>, <code>subaddr_spend</code>, and <code>&lt;i&gt;</code> are known, then <code>master_spend</code> can be derived in the MWEB key derivation design.

This enables import/export canonicalization and the validation strategies below.

===Canonicalization (export) rules===

To prevent multiple encodings of the same underlying wallet material, implementations MUST serialize (export) MWEB descriptors using the following canonical forms:

# '''Ranged wallets'''
#* Always export:
#** <code>mweb(master_scan,master_spend,*)</code>
# '''Single-subaddress wallets'''
#* If <code>master_spend</code> and the subaddress index <code>&lt;i&gt;</code> are known/available:
#** Export: <code>mweb(master_scan,master_spend,&lt;i&gt;)</code>
#* Otherwise (when <code>master_spend</code> or <code>&lt;i&gt;</code> is not known/available, but the subaddress spend key is known):
#** Export: <code>mweb(master_scan,subaddr_spend)</code>

Notes:
* An importer MAY accept non-canonical but semantically equivalent representations if they are ever introduced, but exporters MUST follow the rules above.
* Wallets SHOULD preserve the originally imported form only as metadata; descriptor string output MUST be canonical.

===Validation guidelines===

On import, implementations SHOULD perform the strongest validation possible given the provided fields:

* For <code>mweb(master_scan,master_spend,&lt;i&gt;)</code>:
** Derive the implied subaddress spend key for <code>&lt;i&gt;</code> and ensure internal consistency if the wallet also stores/learns subaddress material.

* For <code>mweb(master_scan,subaddr_spend)</code>:
** No index consistency check is possible by definition.
** The wallet MAY attempt discovery strategies if it later learns <code>master_spend</code> or an index mapping.

* For <code>mweb(master_scan,master_spend,*)</code>:
** Validate literal <code>*</code>.
** If the key material implies derivation paths, validate those paths per existing descriptor key parsing rules.

===Grammar summary===

All tokens are ASCII. No whitespace allowed.

<pre>
mweb_desc :=
    "mweb(" master_scan "," master_spend ",*)" |
    "mweb(" master_scan "," master_spend "," index ")" |
    "mweb(" master_scan "," subaddr_spend ")"

index := DIGIT {DIGIT}

master_scan  := KEY   ; scalar (must be private key)
master_spend := KEY   ; master spend sk or pk
subaddr_spend:= KEY   ; subaddress spend sk or pk
</pre>

Type constraints:
* <code>master_scan</code> MUST represent a scalar (private key material), not a public key.
* <code>master_spend</code> and <code>subaddr_spend</code> MAY be public or private key material.
* In 3-arg forms, the second parameter is '''master''' spend material.
* In the 2-arg form, the second parameter is '''subaddress''' spend material.

===Behavior summary===

{| class="wikitable"
! Descriptor Form !! Range? !! Scan? !! Spend? !! Notes
|-
| <code>mweb(master_scan_sk,master_spend_sk,*)</code> || Yes || Yes || Yes || Full wallet
|-
| <code>mweb(master_scan_sk,master_spend_pk,*)</code> || Yes || Yes || No || Watch-only
|-
| <code>mweb(master_scan_sk,master_spend_sk,i)</code> || No || Yes || Yes || Single subaddress
|-
| <code>mweb(master_scan_sk,master_spend_pk,i)</code> || No || Yes || No || Single view-only
|-
| <code>mweb(master_scan_sk,subaddr_spend_sk)</code> || No || Yes || Yes || Single subaddress
|-
| <code>mweb(master_scan_sk,subaddr_spend_pk)</code> || No || Yes || No || Single view-only
|}

